                    note: "Twisted-pair copper. Cheap, secure, NO RF emission -- but the run caps at ~100 m. The dependable wired default. Unshielded (UTP) and 5.41 mm across, one maker's four-pair 23 AWG Cat6 (Southwire SPEC 13152, R49). Corrected 2026-11-02: it was 6 mm (ConduitKind::DataCable's comment, no sheet) and marked shielded, which a UTP cable is not.",
